WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:05.782
This is the narrated briefing for a
companion guide in the Federal Modernization

3
00:00:05.782 --> 00:00:09.178
Workbook: Service Accounts,
from user accounts to group

4
00:00:09.178 --> 00:00:13.312
managed service accounts to
Microsoft Entra workload identities.

5
00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.874
The guide's idea fits in one line.

6
00:00:15.874 --> 00:00:18.819
A service account's password
is the one nobody changes,

7
00:00:18.819 --> 00:00:20.912
because changing it breaks something.

8
00:00:20.912 --> 00:00:25.042
Every step in the guide replaces a
password someone has to keep with

9
00:00:25.042 --> 00:00:28.876
a credential that Windows, or
Microsoft Entra I D, keeps instead.

10
00:00:28.876 --> 00:00:33.396
Every fact and command in this
deck comes from Microsoft Learn,

11
00:00:33.396 --> 00:00:38.700
read on November ninth and eleventh,
2026, and the guide footnotes each one.

12
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.437
Rules that are the program's own, not
Microsoft's, are called design guidance.

13
00:00:43.437 --> 00:00:48.624
We'll go in four parts: why this matters,
what the kinds of service identity are,

14
00:00:48.624 --> 00:00:52.630
who decides and what they keep,
and how each migration runs.
